eacher.html` page initially sets `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz = false` before asynchronously reading the saved Firestore setting, which could be true.\n\n\nWhen `Auto Record Quiz` is toggled off, the UI should hide the \"Clear Students\" button, submission count badge, and description, displaying a notice instead, while also stopping and aborting any in-flight requests. Conversely, when toggled on, those elements should reappear, and the submission poller should start if the submissions tab is active. The tab-switching logic needs to ensure the poller starts and stops at the correct times. There is a potential need to prevent a race condition involving the auto-record setting's initialization.\n\n\nThe submission poller needs to be immediately cleared and requests aborted upon tab minimization or backgrounding, using `clearInterval` and `subAbort.abort()`. A visibility change listener should be added to ensure the poller cleanly pauses and resumes. Additionally, it's crucial to examine the quiz download settings and template within Firestore, since changes to `index.html` necessitate compiling and hardening both `index.html` and `teacher.html`.\n\n\nThe plan now includes syncing the compiled quiz template to Firestore, ensuring the `autoRecordQuiz` gate applies to offline downloads. A patch entry will be added to the history.md file. Considering the `index.html` file, a check for potential edge cases concerning `isAutoRecord` with missing or undefined settings is underway, with the existing default behavior of defaulting to `true` preserved for backward compatibility.\n\n\nThe `teacher.html` code consistently saves `settings.autoRecordQuiz` as a boolean value, either `true` or `false`. This is confirmed through initialization, merging settings, serialization, and direct inspection of Firestore data. Consequently, the `isAutoRecord()` function in `index.html` reliably receives a boolean value for `autoRecordQuiz` from the settings. Now crafting the `implementation_plan.md` artifact.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Implementation plan to gate remote quiz submissions on autoRecordQuiz in index.html, display the auto-record-only notice while hiding Clear Students and halting polling in teacher.html when autoRecordQuiz is OFF, re-harden and sync the template, and verify all affected flows and callers.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","Content":"\"# Implementation Plan — Gate Submissions by Auto Record Quiz & Add Submissions Notice (`Patch 1.0.23`)\\n\\n## Investigation Summary & Root Cause\\n1. **Unconditional remote submission write in `index.html` (`finish()`):**\\n   - In `tmp_backup/index.html`, `const isAuto = st.autoRecordQuiz !== false;` is evaluated only when updating `#res-actions` / `#res-note`, **after** `EncryptedLocalDB.appendRecord(quizId, subData)` already ran unconditionally.\\n   - Because of this, finishing a quiz on a quiz configured with `autoRecordQuiz: false` (`quizzes/active` currently has `autoRecordQuiz: { booleanValue: false }`) still downloaded `result_*.json` for the student **and** posted a submission document (observed in live Firestore: `1` submission `asd/asd`) to `quizzes/active/submissions`.\\n2. **Unconditional submission polling & display in `teacher.html` (`#view-sub`):**\\n   - `refreshSubmissions()` runs on boot, on tab switch, and every `4000ms` regardless of `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz`, showing stale or inadvertently recorded submissions and displaying the `Clear Students` button (`#clear-sub-btn`) even when Auto Record Quiz is OFF.\\n\\n## Research & Optimization Rationale\\n- **Gated Rest Write & Zero Allocation on Disabled Mode (`index.html`):** Checking `isAutoRecord()` **before** assembling `subData` skips payload object creation, `toStoreFields` Firestore serialization, and the outbound HTTP `POST` altogether when `autoRecordQuiz === false`.\\n- **Single-Source Flag Helper (DRY):** Extracting `isAutoRecord()` removes duplicated inline checks (`st.autoRecordQuiz !== false`) shared between `finish()` and `showLock()`.\\n- **Event-Driven Polling + Cancellation (`teacher.html`):** Following `AbortController` + Visibility API patterns for Firestore REST polling, `syncSubPoller()` runs `setInterval(..., 4000)` only when `settingsState.autoRecordQuiz && !document.hidden && !$('view-sub').classList.contains('hide')`, immediately clears the interval and aborts any in-flight `listRecords()` request when switching tabs, hidin\n<truncated 7508 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\CxAdmin\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\\\implementation_plan.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
